  "notes": "Used across medical, policy, and everyday contexts. Both transitive (to ease something) and intransitive (something eases) uses are common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {規制|きせい}{緩和|かんわ}: deregulation, easing of regulations\n- {金融|きんゆう}{緩和|かんわ}: monetary easing\n- {緩和|かんわ}ケア: palliative care\n- {緊張|きんちょう}{緩和|かんわ}: detente, easing of tensions\n- {痛|いた}みの{緩和|かんわ}: pain relief\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {和|やわ}らげる: to soften, to ease — native Japanese word, more general\n- {緩和|かんわ}する: to ease, to relax — Sino-Japanese, more formal, often used in policy and medical contexts\n- {軽減|けいげん}する: to reduce, to lessen — focuses on making a burden lighter",
